0.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The Court’s decision in McCullen v. Coakley held that the Massachusetts law too broadly restricted speech on public walkways and roads.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"States may still enact more narrowly tailored laws against harassing speech and actions within a clinic “buffer zone”.", "claim_types":["prediction"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"It is not clear whether states that have enacted “buffer zone” legislation will reformulate them.", "claim_types":["prediction"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Support for enacting legislation in every state possible that falls within the parameters defined by the Court decision in McCullen v. Coakley and which also protect women’s rights to unimpeded access to reproductive services.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
